+---
+The gates report 17 findings beyond the ten tags the task names. Every one is
+a tag to a requirement or scenario that this change's own
+`openspec/changes/232-rust-link-gates/specs/rust-linter/spec.md` ADDS
+(`Link gates` and `Live link gates`), so the target is not in the living
+`openspec/specs/rust-linter/spec.md` and cannot become live until this change
+archives. The tags are in files outside this task's scope:
+
+```
+crates/kernel/linter/src/gates.rs:31: Implements: tag names requirement:rust-linter/link-gates, which does not exist
+crates/kernel/linter/src/gates/complete_capabilities.rs:32: Implements: tag names requirement:rust-linter/link-gates, which does not exist
+crates/kernel/linter/src/gates/complete_capabilities.rs:39: Implements: tag names requirement:rust-linter/link-gates, which does not exist
+crates/kernel/linter/src/gates/live_references.rs:34: Implements: tag names requirement:rust-linter/link-gates, which does not exist
+crates/kernel/linter/src/gates/live_references.rs:41: Implements: tag names requirement:rust-linter/link-gates, which does not exist
+crates/kernel/linter/src/gates/owned_once.rs:17: Implements: tag names requirement:rust-linter/link-gates, which does not exist
+crates/kernel/linter/src/gates/owned_once.rs:24: Implements: tag names requirement:rust-linter/link-gates, which does not exist
+crates/kernel/linter/src/gates/tagged_functions.rs:15: Implements: tag names requirement:rust-linter/link-gates, which does not exist
+crates/kernel/linter/src/gates/tagged_functions.rs:22: Implements: tag names requirement:rust-linter/link-gates, which does not exist
+crates/kernel/linter/tests/link_gates.rs:240: Covers: tag names scenario:rust-linter/findings-of-the-link-gates-fixture, which does not exist
+crates/kernel/linter/tests/link_gates.rs:248: Covers: tag names scenario:rust-linter/link-gates-in-another-group, which does not exist
+crates/kernel/linter/tests/link_gates.rs:280: Covers: tag names scenario:rust-linter/link-gate-errors, which does not exist
+crates/kernel/linter/tests/link_gates_corpus.rs:24: Covers: tag names scenario:rust-linter/repository-passes-the-link-gates, which does not exist
+crates/kernel/linter/tests/link_gates_edges.rs:72: Covers: tag names scenario:rust-linter/findings-of-the-link-gates-fixture, which does not exist
+crates/kernel/linter/tests/link_gates_edges.rs:93: Covers: tag names scenario:rust-linter/findings-of-the-link-gates-fixture, which does not exist
+crates/kernel/linter/tests/link_gates_edges.rs:134: Covers: tag names scenario:rust-linter/findings-of-the-link-gates-fixture, which does not exist
+crates/kernel/linter/tests/link_gates_edges.rs:179: Covers: tag names scenario:rust-linter/findings-of-the-link-gates-fixture, which does not exist
+```
+
+Their fix in every case is `Name a living requirement as
+<capability>/<requirement name in kebab-case>.` or `Name a living scenario as
+<capability>/<scenario name in kebab-case>.`
+
+This is a plan-level catch-22, not a code defect the task can fix within its
+scope: ADR 024 makes a tag to a not-yet-living requirement or scenario a
+broken reference, while this change adds the requirements and scenarios its
+own new code tags, and living specs change only when the change archives. One
+of these is needed:
+
+- the corpus test's graph also reads the active change's delta specs, which
+  contradicts `build_link_graph`'s living-spec-only requirement and task 2, or
+- the `Link gates` and `Live link gates` requirements and their scenarios land
+  in an earlier change before this one runs (so the living spec already holds
+  them), or
+- task 3's scope includes the seven `rust-linter` source and test files that
+  carry the new tags, so they can be renamed to existing living requirements
+  (which would then disagree with this change's delta and ADR 024's proposal
+  decision that every new public function is tagged `Implements:
+  rust-linter/link-gates`).
+
+The ten fixes the task specified are done and stay valid under any of the
+three resolutions.
