+## Changed
+
+- Added `crates/kernel/linter/tests/link_gates_corpus.rs`, whose
+  `repository_passes_the_link_gates` test carries
+  `#[ignore = "corpus test: runs the link gates on this repository"]` and
+  `/// Covers: rust-linter/repository-passes-the-link-gates`. It runs
+  `link_gates` on the repository root with `decisions`, `openspec` and group
+  `rust`, and fails on any `complete-capabilities`, `live-references` or
+  `tagged-functions` finding, printing each finding and its fix.
+- Renamed the ten tags of the task table: removed the file tag and the empty
+  `//!` line from `crates/core/tests/event_values.rs`, and renamed the
+  `Covers:` tags in `fold.rs`, `decisions_corpus.rs`, `public_api.rs` (two)
+  and `validating_decisions.rs` (four `Decision finding codes` lines and the
+  `Validation of the decisions fixture` line).
+- With those ten renamed, `cargo test -p osq-kernel-linter --test
+  link_gates_corpus -- --include-ignored` reports no `owned-once`,
+  `complete-capabilities` or `tagged-functions` finding. It still fails on the
+  17 `live-references` findings below.
+
+## Blocked
+
+The gates report 17 findings beyond the ten tags the task names. Every one is
+a tag to a requirement or scenario that this change's own
+`openspec/changes/232-rust-link-gates/specs/rust-linter/spec.md` ADDS
+(`Link gates` and `Live link gates`), so the target is not in the living
+`openspec/specs/rust-linter/spec.md` and cannot become live until this change
+archives. The tags are in files outside this task's scope:
